{"availability":"available","full":"26ds/fermata-app","name":"fermata-app","description":"An active-learning layer for YouTube videos and podcasts: pause anywhere, ask about what was just said, and get answers grounded in the transcript, with bilingual captions and a word bank.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-01T23:50:44Z","updated":"2026-10-02T00:11:53Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://fermata-eta.vercel.app","topics":["edtech","gemini-api","language-learning","llm","nextjs","podcast","postgresql","pwa","react","supabase","tailwindcss","typescript","youtube"],"demo":"https://fermata-eta.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T05:45:02.439Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T05:45:02.439Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T05:45:02.439Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T05:45:02.439Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An active-learning layer for YouTube videos and podcasts. Pause at any moment, ask about what was just said, and get an answer grounded in the transcript. Captions in your own language and the words you save turn watching into studying.","Live demo: It runs in desktop browsers for now (phones get an \"open this on a computer\" screen). Sign in with Google.","Most of what we learn from video is watched passively and forgotten. A good lecture, a long interview or a talk in a language you're learning raises questions at a specific second, and there is nobody to ask. Fermata puts a tutor at that second. It knows what was just said, can point you to the other places the video covers it, and keeps the words and moments you want to come back to."],"features":["Ask about this moment. Pause anywhere and type a question. The answer is based on the seconds you just heard plus the full transcript, and it remembers the conversation.","Ask about another moment with @12:34, @754 or @-13 (13 seconds back). The video stays where it is.","Capture points. Every question, or a quick \"Just mark this moment\", leaves a dot on the timeline under the video. Click one to jump back to that second.","Captions that fill in while you watch. Long videos are transcribed in slices and shown as they arrive. Each video is transcribed once and then shared with everyone who opens it.","A workbench for a wide screen. Three layouts (Focus captions, Immersive · narrow, Immersive · wide) with draggable dividers keep the video, the captions and your questions on one screen."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/26ds/fermata-app/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e4615a5c97c8751df7880c943d25b07a403eb91ef28c1a52ffa89d051e75f216","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T05:45:02.612Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T05:45:02.612Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An active-learning layer for YouTube videos and podcasts. Pause at any moment, ask about what was just said, and get an answer grounded in the transcript. Captions in your own language and the words you save turn watching into studying.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/26ds/fermata-app/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Sign in with Google.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/26ds/fermata-app/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"e4615a5c97c8751df7880c943d25b07a403eb91ef28c1a52ffa89d051e75f216","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/26ds/fermata-app/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T05:45:02.613Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-02T00:11:53Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/26ds/fermata-app/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T05:45:02.613Z","hash":"e4615a5c97c8751df7880c943d25b07a403eb91ef28c1a52ffa89d051e75f216","originalBytes":11674,"storedBytes":11674,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["api","supabase","video","transcript","captions","answer","every","gemini","src","what","ask","language","lib","only","word","back","line",